VERDICT
========================================================================
  LIKELY VULNERABLE (worker crashed on oversized POST; pre-fix build reported)
  An oversized text field crashed the worker while small POSTs succeeded, and PHP reports ['8.5.11'] (vulnerable) — a pre-fix build. On pre-fix 8.5.11 an rfc1867 OOM is fatal and not recovered, which is exactly this crash.
  oversized POST: 16 MB, HTTP 500, 0.01s

  MITIGATIONS (patching is the only complete fix — 8.5.12 / 8.4.27 / 8.3.36 / 8.2.35):
    * Update PHP, then restart / replace every PHP worker.
    * memory_limit=-1 administratively (php_admin_value) — removes the
      predictable memory-limit trigger (check no pool/dir/app restores it).
    * session.upload_progress.enabled=0 in php.ini / FPM / server config
      applied BEFORE request parsing — ini_set() and .user.ini are too late.
    * PHP 8.5: fatal_error_backtraces=0 administratively.
    * FPM: pm.max_requests=1 interrupts cross-request chains (perf cost).
    * Edge limits on decoded request size, multipart parts, nesting depth.

  Authorization reminder: probes are visible in access logs.
  Run only on targets you own or are authorized to test.

